{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1036037-question-about-the-huntsman","id":1036037,"title":"Question about the Huntsman","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-22T06:35:30-08:00","id":1036037,"title":"Question about the Huntsman","content":"As far as we know, Huntsmen are implacable pursuers who absolutely <b>won\u00b4t</b> stop until they prey is captured. Does that mean the moment one of them appears in the Chronicle after one of the PCs, his player\u00b4s only options are: a) be eventually captured or b) sell out another changeling(s) for a token?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T06:55:14-08:00","id":1036042,"title":"","content":"in many ways, that is life for a changeling: constantly dealing with Huntsmen. There will be respites when they cause them to run out of Yearning or even get a Token of Reprieve (though not sure if that makes them forever off limits, but they are prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:03:26-08:00","id":1036102,"title":"","content":"Another option does involve killing the Huntsmen, and in fact one of the pre-made courts even makes such a hunt part of their rituals. However, the problem with that is that a Huntsman kills a human every time they come from the Hedge, so as to adapt to Ironside, and they need to repeat this when they come back over once they're killed. Since they're the spirits of Arcadia made flesh, they simply return to Arcadia and are sent back out again at a later point.<br /> <br /> I don't think imprisonment was ever concieved as an option for Huntsmen, but then again, they tend to be difficult to capture, much less imprison. Fae in general are difficult to hold against their will outside of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Also, I noted elsewhere that while the book notes &quot;a significant number of Changelings take the token&quot;, this doesn't mean MOST or even half of them. A significant number just means that it's a number high enough to be significant, and in this context it probably means simply being more than what you'd want for the Changeling population. If a quarter of your apples become bruised before you can sell them, that's a significant amount because those ones aren't viable for being sold, but it doesn't mean the shipment is not going to get you back money. Likewise, if a fifth of the population of a city is homophobic, that's a significant number of people for an archaic and detrimental line of thought and badly reflects on the city, even if the remaining eighty percent is perfectly accepting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:04:14-08:00","id":1036103,"title":"","content":"A) Get Captured<br /> B) Sell Out<br /> C) Survive the Time Limit<br /> D) Unmake the Huntsman<br /> E) Other Options I can't think of Because I'm just awoken.<br /> <br /> I have doubled your list, at the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:54:00-08:00","id":1036134,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that if you manage to &quot;kill the huntsmen&quot; they would take a fortnight to recover","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:04:40-08:00","id":1036139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1036037-question-about-the-huntsman?p=1036103#post1036103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) Get Captured<br /> B) Sell Out<br /> C) Survive the Time Limit<br /> D) Unmake the Huntsman<br /> E) Other Options I can't think of Because I'm just awoken.<br /> <br /> I have doubled your list, at the least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is no Time Limit. A Hunstman cannot be free from his Keeper\u00b4s service until he brings back the runaway changeling, or a token of reprieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:28:28-08:00","id":1036188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1036037-question-about-the-huntsman?p=1036139#post1036139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is no Time Limit. A Hunstman cannot be free from his Keeper\u00b4s service until he brings back the runaway changeling, or a token of reprieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not Huntsman need to be called in first place by a Keeper? This would mean that you need to piss your once Keeper in the first place - things I would think start at the Wyrd 3 at very least, maybe at Wyrd 5 for the changeling. Most of the time, fresh running changelings are too low fish to fry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:45:24-08:00","id":1036201,"title":"","content":"I thought they formed sort of 'naturally' in response to the changeling's escape. It might be a True Fae wanting them back but it didn't sound like a knowing summoning is necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:34:49-08:00","id":1036221,"title":"","content":"i'm pretty sure they are created specifically by True Fae. You might be confusing them with the Huntsmen archetype mentioned in 1e. That was a type of True Fae that was more primal, engaging in the Wild Hunt and disdaining the rigid rules of Gentry interactions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\